# The single-file apps briefly contained control bytes (a regex-cache key and a
# clause-splitter sentinel), which made git classify them as BINARY. While that
# flag was set, core.autocrlf stopped normalizing them, so CRLF endings were
# committed verbatim into files the rest of the repo stores as LF. Every line
# then read as changed: a one-line edit produced a 25,000-line diff and merging
# main became one whole-file conflict. Declaring them text pins the repo copy to
# LF regardless of what the heuristic decides, so this cannot recur.
*.html text
*.js   text
*.mjs  text
*.json text
*.md   text

*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.docx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
